  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The root mean square velocity of molecules of gas is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GojQP",
      "text": "Proportional to square of temperature (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>).",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GSMcr",
      "text": "Inversely proportional to square root of&nbsp;temperature (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>).",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "QFbTp",
      "text": "Proportional to square root of temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s7ELX",
      "text": "Proportional to temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Root mean&nbsp;speed of a gas molecule is stated as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is the universal gas constant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is&nbsp;temperature, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is the molar&nbsp;mass of the gas.</p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>&#8733;</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
